---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import ButtonLink from '../../components/ButtonLink.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Document compliance review | Jorge Buckley"
  description="Case study: turning document review into an actionable product workflow with React and Python APIs."
>
  <Container class="space-y-10" width="narrow">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] m-0">Professional case study · Complete</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        Turning document review into an actionable product workflow
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        A product flow that helped reviewers check marketing documents against approved language and find problems faster.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="context-heading">
      <h2 id="context-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Context</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Marketing content had to be checked against approved language and offer details. Reviewers were dealing with multi-page documents and needed a clearer path from upload to a usable finding.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="challenge-heading">
      <h2 id="challenge-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Challenge</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Documents had to be processed, discrepancies surfaced clearly, and reviewers directed back to the right source material without digging through every page by hand.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="role-heading">
      <h2 id="role-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Role</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        I worked on the React experience and Python APIs that extracted text from PDFs and images, then presented comparison results in the UI. Broader product and platform work was a team effort.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
      <h2 id="approach-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Approach</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        <li>Supported document upload and extraction so reviewers weren't stuck in a manual copy-paste loop.</li>
        <li>Compared extracted content against approved language and surfaced discrepancies in the UI.</li>
        <li>Linked findings back toward the approved source material so reviewers could act on them.</li>
        <li>Kept product names, volumes, and internal architecture out of this public write-up.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="result-heading">
      <h2 id="result-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Result</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Reviewers got a structured way to find discrepancies and locate approved language, instead of hunting through documents alone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="demonstrates-heading">
      <h2 id="demonstrates-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        What this shows
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        Complex workflow design, React UI work, Python APIs, document processing, and results people can explain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="tech-heading">
      <h2 id="tech-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">Technologies</h2>
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 list-none m-0 p-0">
        {['React', 'TypeScript', 'Python', 'Document AI / OCR', 'REST APIs'].map((tag) => (
          <li class="px-2 py-1 bg-[color:var(--color-luxe-card)] border border-[color:var(--color-luxe-border)] text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)] rounded text-sm">
            {tag}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section
      class="bg-[color:var(--color-luxe-card)] border border-[color:var(--color-luxe-border)] rounded-lg p-6 space-y-4"
      aria-labelledby="cs-cta-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="cs-cta-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-luxe-text)]">
        Need a complex workflow UI?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-subtext)]">
        I help teams turn messy review processes into clear product flows.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <ButtonLink href="/services#react-product" umamiEvent="case-compliance-services">
          View React service
        </ButtonLink>
        <ButtonLink href="/contact" variant="secondary" umamiEvent="case-compliance-contact">
          Get in touch
        </ButtonLink>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p>
      <a
        href="/work"
        class="text-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] hover:underline focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[color:var(--color-luxe-accent)] rounded"
      >
        ← Back to work
      </a>
    </p>
  </Container>
</Layout>
